<!--Post: 6833--><!--Time: 1108032898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6833"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 2:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Last night, KAKE aired original tapes from the 70&#39;s when BTK just started his rampage.  Even though it was illegal &#40;usually&#41; the PD got permission to run a subliminal spot.  KAKE showed the tape at normal speed and then stopped it so the subliminal picture could be seen. <BR> <BR>I have a hunch &#40;quite likely wrong&#41; that the illustration shown - one of a simple line drawing of glasses - could be the &#39;secret symbol&#39; found on BTK&#39;s correspondence.   <BR> <BR>I know the PD did some investigating of &#39;glasses&#39; with their subjects but it seems strange to tie victims together simply because they wear glasses. <BR> <BR>Any thoughts?   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6833-->
<!--Post: 6834--><!--Time: 1108034673-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6834"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 3:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Take a look at the baby picture - at the corner that was cut off.  There is just a little squiggle left. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/btkbaby.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/btkbaby.html</a> <BR> <BR>But, it could be the tail end of one of the earpieces of the glasses.  Compare here: <BR> <BR><a href="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v649/SupermanBatman/CallTheChief.jpg" target=_top>http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v649/SupermanBat man/CallTheChief.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6834-->
<!--Post: 6872--><!--Time: 1108058043-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6872"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Maxgravis<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Maxgravis<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 9:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting, I wonder if BTK will give us all the answers when he is caught &#40; or turns himself in after WPD cannot find him&#41;. We all have probably made much more of all the riddles and clues than need be. I bet BTK gives a map to his house and WPD still can&#39;t find him &#40;Oh, did you mean East or West 61st&#41; <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6872-->
<!--Post: 6877--><!--Time: 1108059590-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6877"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 10:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thise &#34;glasess&#34; are very odd IMO in fact they look more like a clone between a pair if stirrups and a pair of glasses. And IMO noone, not even a person with the worst thinkeable drawing skills would draw a pair of glasses/sunglasses like that. It is the FORM of the glasses frames that are SO far from what any glasses look like. <BR>One could also see the glasess frames as a big B letter lying down? <BR>Well I have no sugestion what it should mean I just wanted to share my thoughts. <BR>Anyone else see the same thing as I or somthing else? <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6877-->
<!--Post: 6890--><!--Time: 1108063709-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6890"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Aren&#39;t the wrap around backs the ones that are used for children who need glasses?  The drawing does look very very strange...but I have seen children&#39;s glasses made this way with the wrap around the ear part so that they aren&#39;t constantly loosing or damaging their glasses while they are playing??????? At least back when I was young in the 50&#39;s &amp; 60&#39;s that&#39;s how kids glasses were...I don&#39;t know if they still make them that way.  The Lenses are very strange also, maybe they are very thick, perhaps SOMEONE has &#40;had&#41; extremely poor eyesight.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6890-->
<!--Post: 6929--><!--Time: 1108080204-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6929"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 4:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It struck me as interesting that the glasses are drawn in such detail.  It isn&#39;t just a quick squiggle.  If the glasses graphic was from a drawing made by BTK, it would make sense for the rest of his drawings to be in great detail &#40;which apparently they are, right down to items on Nancy Fox&#39;s dresser&#41;.   <BR> <BR>BTK is a practiced drawer, whatever we may think of his artistic skills, and he probably sketched a lot when he was young.  He may have taken an art class or done some cartooning or something similar.  Hard to say if anyone who knew him only as an adult would know anything about his drawing hobby.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6929-->
<!--Post: 6931--><!--Time: 1108081186-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6931"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 4:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When I saw this video with Lt Kenneth Landwehr I struck me that his glasess looked very simelar to those &#34;BTK&#34; glasess, and Lt KL´s glasess lokes like 70-80th glasess, maybe BTK wore that kind of glases? <BR>OR did Lt KL also have that kind of glases back then and BTK draw them to taunt the police/Landwehr? indicating symbolicly that they needed &#34;new glasess&#34; to find BTK <BR> <BR>here is the video to compare: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6620172.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/6620172.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6931-->
